zl1 -- the modem's door: readings and the fix, 2026-09-25
=========================================================

One boot throughout: boot_id 2fbf9f8e-deea-4955-ad0c-6bddf0fb14f5 (read before and after every
step below; it did not change). No partition was written, no block device was opened, nothing was
rebooted, and the Android container was never stopped.

Everything here was read from the device over ssh (root@10.15.19.82, the rndis0 address), except
where a line is marked otherwise.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A. THE MODEM WAS NEVER MISSING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  /sys/class/remoteproc does not exist (3.18 kernel)
  msm_subsys modem: state=ONLINE   crash_count=0   error=(empty)
  /vendor/firmware_mnt/image: modem.mdt=present modem.b00=present mba.mbn=present
  no firmware-load failure line in this boot's kernel log
  pil-q6v5-mss 2080000.qcom,mss: Failed to find the pas_id.     (dev_warn, optional property,
                                                                 non-fatal -- see docs 120)

  ANDROID'S RADIO HAL IS REGISTERED AND LIVE, in lshal's FIRST table (the table whose `R` column
  is the one that means anything; doc 149). `nsenter -t 35320 -p -m -- lshal`, line 43 of 246:

    Y android.hardware.radio@1.1::IRadio/slot1
    Y android.hardware.radio@1.1::IRadio/slot2

  Every radio HAL version this device registers, and only these:

    android.hardware.radio@1.0::IRadio/slot1, /slot2
    android.hardware.radio@1.0::ISap/slot1, /slot2
    android.hardware.radio@1.1::IRadio/slot1, /slot2
    android.hardware.radio@1.1::ISap/slot1, /slot2
    android.hardware.radio.deprecated@1.0::IOemHook/slot1, /slot2

  rild is running: container pids 372, 466 and 815 (`/vendor/bin/hw/rild`, `rild -c 2`), and
  /dev/subsys_modem is held by /vendor/bin/pm-service.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
B. DOOR 1 -- THE PLUGIN WAS THE WRONG ONE, AND THE CHOICE WAS MADE BY A CRASH
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The running ofonod before the fix, from its own cmdline:

  /usr/sbin/ofonod -P stktest,sap,udev,dun,smart,hfp,hfp_bluez5,provision,binder --nodetach

`-P` disables, and `binder` is in the list -- so the binder plugin is off and the ril plugin is on.
Confirmed from /proc/<pid>/maps of the running ofonod (the four .so files it had mapped):

  apndbplugin.so
  mtkbinderpluginext.so
  qtibinderpluginext.so
  rilbinderplugin.so
  rilplugin.so
  (binderplugin.so: NOT mapped)

Why the wrapper picks ril: /etc/systemd/system/ofono.service.d/lxc-android-config.conf replaces
ExecStart with /usr/libexec/lxc-android-config/ofonod-wrapper, whose plugin choice is

  if [ "$(device-info get OfonoPlugin)" = "binder" ]; then ... else "disable binder, use ril"

and on this port that command does not answer, it dies:

  $ device-info get OfonoPlugin
  Segmentation fault   (rc=139)

  $ for k in DeviceName DeviceType OfonoPlugin SensorfwConfig NoSuchKeyAtAll; do
      device-info get "$k"; echo "rc=$?"
    done
  DeviceName       rc=139
  PrettyName       rc=139
  DeviceType       rc=139
  OfonoPlugin      rc=139
  SensorfwConfig   rc=139
  NoSuchKeyAtAll   rc=139

Every key, every environment (`env -i`, `HOME=`, `QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen`): rc=139.

Where it dies -- `strace -f device-info get DeviceType`, last seven syscalls:

  newfstatat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/__properties__", {st_mode=S_IFDIR|0711, st_size=3340, ...}, 0) = 0
  faccessat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/__properties__/property_info", R_OK) = 0
  openat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/__properties__/property_info", O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC) = 3
  mmap(NULL, 26812, PROT_READ, MAP_SHARED, 3, 0) = 0x6fdcb68000
  openat(AT_FDCWD, "/dev/__properties__/properties_serial", O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_CLOEXEC) = 3
  mmap(NULL, 131072, PROT_READ, MAP_SHARED, 3, 0) = 0x6fdc450000
  --- SIGSEGV {si_signo=SIGSEGV, si_code=SEGV_MAPERR, si_addr=0xb00} ---
  +++ killed by SIGSEGV +++

  `ltrace -f` puts the same crash inside `DeviceInfo::DeviceInfo(PrintMode)` -- the constructor,
  before any answer is printed. The binary itself is intact (`dpkg -V deviceinfo-tools` checksums
  it clean; only its man page is missing), and the property area it maps is real and shared: the
  host's /dev/__properties__ is the container's (same directory inode 46277, same 165 files, and
  the container's mountinfo shows it as `master:72` of the host's `shared:72`).

  So the property area is not the problem; **a host process simply cannot complete an Android
  property read here**. The same crash, from a different program, with the same shape:

    python3 -c "import ctypes; lib=ctypes.CDLL('/lib/aarch64-linux-gnu/libandroid-properties.so.1');
                lib.property_get(b'ro.product.device', buf, None)"
    Segmentation fault

  while inside the container the same question has a real answer:

    nsenter -t 35320 -p -m -- /system/bin/getprop ro.product.device   ->  le_zl1
    nsenter -t 35320 -p -m -- sh -c '/system/bin/getprop | wc -l'     ->  695

Why the ril plugin cannot be the answer, even if it were chosen correctly:

  /etc/ofono/ril_subscription.conf's only active keys:
      [Settings]
      [ril_0]
      socket=/dev/socket/rild

  $ ls -l /dev/socket/rild
  ls: cannot access '/dev/socket/rild': No such file or directory

  $ ls /dev/socket/qmux_radio/
  qcril_radio_config0  qcril_radio_config1  rild_sync_0  rild_sync_1

  $ cat /var/lib/lxc/android/rootfs/vendor/etc/init/rild.legacy.rc
  service ril-daemon /vendor/bin/hw/rild
      class main
      user radio
      group radio cache inet misc audio log readproc wakelock
      capabilities BLOCK_SUSPEND NET_ADMIN NET_RAW

  That is the whole file, and it is the ONLY file in the vendor image that mentions rild. There is
  no `socket rild` directive anywhere, so Android never creates /dev/socket/rild and ofono's ril
  plugin can never connect. The device's own journal says so, 11 times in this boot, in the words
  of the old ofono:

    ofonod-wrapper[37946]: [grilio-socket] ERROR: Can't connect to RILD: No such file or directory

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C. DOOR 2 -- THE NAMESPACE (the fifth service behind the same wall)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The identical ofonod command line, run twice, changing only the namespace:

  host namespace:
    ofonod[1950681]: Initializing RIL binder transport plugin.
    ofonod[1950681]: Terminating
    [gbinder] WARNING: registerForNotifications(android.hardware.radio.config@1.0::IRadioConfig) failed

  container PID namespace (`zl1-ns-exec`):
    ofonod[11762]: Initializing RIL binder transport plugin.
    ofonod[11762]: Missing path for slot slot1
    ofonod[11762]: Missing path for slot slot2

  Same binary, same config, same arguments. In the container the plugin got as far as enumerating
  the slots from hwservicemanager; from the host it could not register for anything.

  For completeness, the device nodes are not the difference -- both namespaces open the same ones:

    host:      /dev/binder 15430  /dev/hwbinder 15431  /dev/vndbinder 15432
    container: /dev/binder 15430  /dev/hwbinder 15431  /dev/vndbinder 15432

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
D. DOOR 3 -- THE CONFIG
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

With the plugin and the namespace right, the plugin still refused:

  ofonod[...]: Missing path for slot slot1
  ofonod[...]: Missing path for slot slot2

`binderplugin.so` reads /etc/ofono/binder.conf (its strings: `binder.conf`, `[slotN]`, `path`,
`radioInterface`, `extPlugin`, `ExpectSlots`, `IgnoreSlots`, `Device`, `InterfaceType`), and
upstream (mer-hybris/ofono-binder-plugin, © Jolla Ltd. 2021-2022, the same copyright as the
installed package) documents the two things that matter here:

  * "For reliable startup, /etc/ofono/binder.conf has to list all expected slots"
  * "The exceptions are "path" and "slot" values which must be unique and therefore must appear in
     the section(s) for the respective slot(s)"
  * `radioInterface` -- "Default 1.2 (android.hardware.radio@1.2::IRadio)"

and this device registers only 1.0 and 1.1 (section A above).

The file does not exist on this port, and /etc/ofono is on the read-only image: it is NOT among
the paths /etc/fstab binds from /userdata (`grep ofono /etc/fstab` matches only
`/var/lib/ofono`, which is ofono's storage, not its config).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
E. THE EXPERIMENT -- a private bus, a tmpfs overlay, and two modems
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Run before anything was installed, with /etc/ofono overlaid by a tmpfs (umounted afterwards, the
image's three files copied back first) so that nothing persisted:

  [Settings]
  ExpectSlots=slot1,slot2

  [slot1]
  path=/ril_0
  radioInterface=1.1

  [slot2]
  path=/ril_1
  radioInterface=1.1

  DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS=unix:path=$B /userdata/zl1-hybris/bin/zl1-ns-exec \
      /usr/sbin/ofonod -n -P stktest,sap,udev,dun,smart,hfp,hfp_bluez5,provision,ril,rilbinder
  ...
  [gbinder-radio] Connected to android.hardware.radio@1.1::IRadio/slot1
  [gbinder-radio] Connected to android.hardware.radio@1.1::IRadio/slot2
  ... (the "Missing path" lines are gone)

  busctl --address=unix:path=$B call org.ofono / org.ofono.Manager GetModems
  a(oa{sv}) 2
    "/ril_0" 10 "Online" b false "Powered" b true "Lockdown" b false "Emergency" b false
             "Revision" s "MPSS.TH.2.0.c1.9.1-00044" "Serial" s "861579037654648"
             "SoftwareVersionNumber" s "00"
             "Interfaces" as 4 org.ofono.VoiceCallManager org.ofono.SimManager
                               org.nemomobile.ofono.CellInfo org.nemomobile.ofono.SimInfo
             "Features" as 1 "sim"  "Type" s "hardware"
    "/ril_1" ... "Serial" s "861579037654655" ...

Before this, on every boot of this port, the same call answered `a(oa{sv}) 0`.

  $ umount /etc/ofono && ls /etc/ofono/
  main.conf  phonesim.conf  ril_subscription.conf          (the image's own files, back)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
F. THE INSTALL (scripts/hybris-shims/install-ofono-binder.sh --install)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything it wrote, and nothing else:

  /userdata/zl1-ofono/etc/{main.conf,phonesim.conf,ril_subscription.conf,binder.conf}
  /etc/systemd/system/ofono.service.d/zz-zl1-ofono.conf

The drop-in:

  [Service]
  BindPaths=/userdata/zl1-ofono/etc:/etc/ofono
  Environment=OFONO_SYSTEM_APNDB_PATH=/usr/share/lineageos-apndb/apns-conf.xml
  ExecStart=
  ExecStart=/userdata/zl1-hybris/bin/zl1-ns-exec /usr/sbin/ofonod -P stktest,sap,udev,dun,smart,hfp,hfp_bluez5,provision,ril,rilplugin,rilbinder,rilbinderplugin --nodetach

`BindPaths=` gives ofonod a private mount namespace in which /etc/ofono is the writable copy --
nothing is mounted globally and no other process sees a different /etc/ofono. The namespace is
inherited by zl1-ns-exec's child, because that wrapper enters the PID namespace and never the
mount one.

Its verification, 12 s after `systemctl restart ofono` on the REAL system bus:

  unit:     active  (1973204)
  cmdline:  /userdata/zl1-hybris/bin/zl1-ns-exec /usr/sbin/ofonod -P ...ril,rilplugin,rilbinder,rilbinderplugin --nodetach
  GetModems: a(oa{sv}) 2 "/ril_0" 10 "Online" b false "Powered" b true ... "Serial" s "861579037654648"

and the journal for this boot, in order -- the old ofono's last words, then the new one:

