--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
H. WHAT IS NOT ESTABLISHED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * NO SIM. `org.ofono.SimManager.GetProperties` on /ril_0 answers

        a{sv} 1 "Present" b false

    Whether that is an empty tray or a detection gap is NOT established here. The one knob that
    was deliberately left unset is `extPlugin` (the QTI extension, `qtibinderpluginext.so` is
    installed and currently loaded standalone); on Qualcomm devices it is what carries IMS/VoLTE
    specifics and it is the obvious next thing to try if a SIM is known to be inserted.
    The Android side could not be asked either way: `getprop` inside the container answers 695
    properties, but none of them match gsm.sim.* / gsm.operator.*, and an absent key is not an
    answer about the SIM.

  * `Power request failed`, once, 30 s after ofono started (binder plugin). "Online b true" came
    anyway, and "Powered" never went false.

  * PERSISTENCE ACROSS A REBOOT IS NOT MEASURED. Both files it writes are on the persistent ext4
    (/etc/systemd/system is a bind of /userdata/system-data/etc/systemd/system, and /userdata is
    /dev/sda10), and ofono's drop-in is the same mechanism a dozen zl1-* units already use at
    boot -- but no cold boot has been done since the install.

  * Nothing else was re-read while this was being done: camera, GPS and fingerprint are where
    the previous reading left them (docs 123, 166, 167).
